# Forms & Scoring

Audit forms are category → question → option trees; submissions are scored by a
shared engine used in both preview and final scoring.

## Frontend engine (`frontend/src/utils/forms/`)

- `formBuilder.ts` — build/normalize form definitions.
- `formRenderer.ts`, `formRenderPrep.ts`, `formRenderTypes.ts` — render pipeline.
- `formRendererComponents.tsx` — canonical question widgets. `YesNoQuestion`,
  `RadioQuestion`, `MultiSelectQuestion`, and the `optionCls` pill pattern live
  here. REUSE `optionCls` for any "pick one of N" UI — do not hand-roll radios.
- `completedFormRenderer.tsx`, `scoreRenderer.tsx` — read-only completed views.
- `scoringEngine.ts`, `rollupEngine.ts` — the single source of truth for scores
  and category/question rollups. Do not duplicate scoring math elsewhere; call these.
- `formConditions.ts` — conditional-display rule evaluation.
- `formValidation.ts` — form-level validation.

## Backend

Form definition CRUD is in `backend/src/controllers/form.controller.ts` +
`FormService`; follow [.cursor/rules/backend-api-conventions.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/backend-api-conventions.mdc).

## Scope note

This rule covers the **form-definition + scoring engine** only. The
**submission / dispute** workflow that consumes a scored form
(`SubmissionService`, `services/qa/**`, `dispute.controller.ts`, the
submission-detail pages) lives in its own map:
[.cursor/rules/submissions-disputes.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/submissions-disputes.mdc).

